    Concentric 1-cell-thick rectangular rings filling the entire grid.
    Layer depth d = min(row, col, N-1-row, N-1-col). Depths 0..N/2-1.
    Every cell at the same depth has the same color. Innermost layer is 2x2.
  colors: N/2 distinct non-black (1-9) colors, one per layer
  rule: reverse the color sequence from outermost to innermost layer
  output: same geometry, color at depth d becomes color at depth (N/2-1-d)

